    "sourceNotes": "BA-RUS in the 2026–2027 catalogue and OER Articles 2.2, 2.3, 2.9 and 4.2 establish the 180 EC illustration. First-listed Politics, History and Economics is used consistently in years two and three. Year two includes 10 EC of Russian language study abroad, 5 EC of art history in Daugavpils and a separate 5 EC language acquisition course. The required zero-credit thesis seminar is recorded outside the credit total. The thesis catalogue states completion of years one and two. The adopted OER requires the first year and second-year disciplinary seminars and excludes the listed language and abroad units from the formal gate. This route completes both earlier years, satisfying both.",
