  "exception": {
    "type": "no-defensible-ucr-match",
    "checkedOn": "2026-11-06",
    "reason": "UCR offers literary interpretation, film and documentary analysis, modern history and comparative politics. These courses can introduce selected material on the Russian Revolution, the Soviet period and Russian cinema. Leiden develops Russian language skills alongside sustained study of Russian literature, history, politics and society, and requires Russian-language sources in the final thesis. UCR’s available courses cover parts of that subject matter without the sustained regional study and source work that organize the Leiden degree.",
    "curriculumContext": "The illustrated Politics, History and Economics route combines Russian language study and regional coursework, including study in Daugavpils, with 30 EC of third-year electives and a 10 EC thesis. The separately listed thesis seminar carries no additional credits.",
    "ucrCourseEvidence": "Two internal 24-course schedules passed current workbook feasibility. Literature and cultural analysis tests textual interpretation, film adaptation, documentary, art, stylistics and psycholinguistics. History and political economy tests modern history, empires, comparative politics, international relations, law, macroeconomics, public economics and econometrics. Isolated coverage of Russia and Soviet material is academically relevant. Neither schedule supports sustained regional scholarship or research with Russian-language sources. The description-only American Century seminar provides historical inquiry methods rather than Soviet regional coverage.",
    "candidateAssessment": [
      {
